    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "A synonym is a word or phrase that means exactly or nearly the same as another word in the same language.",
        "Words often carry subtle shades of meaning, so choosing the correct synonym requires analyzing sentence context.",
        "Etymology, root words, prefixes, and suffixes serve as critical tools for eliminating incorrect choices.",
        "A common exam error is selecting an antonym or a visually similar distractor word instead of the true synonym."
      ],
      "id": "v0epeik"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Always verify the part of speech (noun, verb, adjective) of the given word to narrow down option choices.",
        "Watch out for option traps that list exact antonyms, which test your attention under time pressure.",
        "Evaluate the degree of intensity—choose the closest option in tone and severity when multiple near-synonyms are presented."
      ],
      "id": "tnpxvod"
    },
